-- title:
--   Integrality of p/(jₚ-jᵖ) and a simple zero at supersingular a
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and a field $\bar F$ that is a $k$-algebra. Let $C$ be a `ComponentChart` for $A$ and the field $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar p`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$p$ modular function field; thus $C$ consists of a valuation subring `C.integers` of $F$, a surjective reduction map `C.residue` onto $\bar F$ with kernel the maximal ideal, a set of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a finite set of nodes among the places of $\bar F$ over $k$, and a map from places of $F$ to places of $\bar F$, subject to the chart axioms. Let $X \in \bar F$ and let $c \mapsto \mathrm{xpl}(c)$ assign to each $c \in k$ a place of $\bar F$ over $k$, such that for every $c$ and every polynomial $P$ over $k$ one has $\mathrm{ord}_{\mathrm{xpl}(c)}(P(X)) = \mathrm{mult}_c(P)$, the root multiplicity of $c$ in $P$ (ord being minus the logarithm of the associated $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation). Assume the element $j$ of $F$ coming from the $q$-expansion `jq`, and the element $j_p$ coming from `qExpand ℚ p jq` (substitution $q \mapsto q^p$), both lie in `C.integers`, with reductions $X$ and $X^p$ respectively. Assume $p \ge 5$, and let $a \in k$ satisfy: $a$ lies in `ssJSet p k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero point killed by $p$; $a^{p^2} = a$; $a \ne 0$; $a \ne 1728$. The conclusion is that the element $p\,(j_p - j^{\,p})^{-1}$ of $F$ (with $p$ taken via the structure map from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) lies in `C.integers`, and that its reduction under `C.residue` has order exactly $1$ at the place $\mathrm{xpl}(a)$.
--
--   This is the quantitative form, on the chart of the component of $X_0(p)$ in characteristic $p$ through the cusp $\infty$, of the statement that $p/(j_p-j^{\,p})$ is a parameter for the opposite annulus at a supersingular point $a$: by Kronecker's congruence for the modular polynomial $\Phi_p$ the reduction of this function has a simple zero at $X = a$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.isAttached_oppAnnulus_inftyChart_of_chartSpec_univ`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isAttached_oppAnnulus_inftyChart_of_chartSpec_univ) to attach the supersingular annuli of $X_0(p)$ to the infinity chart.
